tickets.body:
The Metrics dashboard and the MCP metrics tools need one project-level read model so the desktop and agents see identical numbers.

Add `getMetricsSummary` to the shared command API (`CommandApi` in `src/shared/domain/api.ts`; capability `read` in `COMMAND_CAPABILITIES`, `src/core/commands/capabilities.ts`). Implement it in core on top of the scorecard read models from DM-178 and DM-179: no second calculation layer, no renderer-side regrading, no averaging of letters.

Input: optional `epicIds` filter and optional observation window (`since`/`until`, ISO 8601). Output, typed in `src/shared/domain/views.ts`:
- policy version and observation cutoff;
- per-epic rows: epic id/title/status, grade (numeric, letter, status final/provisional/ungraded/in-progress/failed), coverage, normalized token categories plus a derived total only where semantics permit, elapsed/active/waiting time, summed effort, corrective share, sprint count;
- project totals recomputed from raw measures, and a grade-status distribution that counts final, provisional and ungraded separately;
- a per-sprint trend ordered by end time, with each entry flagged comparable or not (policy, cohort, observation window);
- top gaps: lowest components and failure/rework causes with evidence and ticket ids;
- data coverage, with unavailable fields explicit (null plus a reason), never zero.

Expose it to the renderer through the existing generic command channel: add `getMetricsSummary` to the `DESKTOP_COMMANDS` allowlist in `src/shared/desktop/api.ts`; the renderer calls `window.dm.command(folder, 'getMetricsSummary', input)`, and `src/main/desktop/handlers.ts` refuses untracked folders through `requireTracked`. Add no new IPC channel and no change to `ipc.ts`, the preload or `window.d.ts`.

New commands: add them to `COMMAND_FLAGS` in `src/test/stubApi.ts` (typecheck requires it). `src/mcp/server.test.ts` asserts that every command outside `HUMAN_ONLY` and `DESKTOP_READS` has an MCP tool, so put desktop-only mutations in `HUMAN_ONLY` and the new reads in `DESKTOP_READS` until DM-266 adds their tools, then run `npx vitest run src/mcp/server.test.ts`. The MCP adapter is DM-266; the dashboard is DM-267.

Delivery (fast lane, this epic only): implement; do not write or extend tests in this ticket. By the owner's decision for this epic, test authoring for this ticket's behavior is consolidated into the testing tickets at the end of the sprint, which name this ticket and its criteria. Verify with `npm run typecheck`, `npx oxlint <files you touched>` and the existing Vitest files for the modules you touched (`npx vitest run <those files>`), fixing any you broke. Demonstrate each acceptance criterion with a short script under `scratch/<this ticket's key>/` (repository root, outside `src/`, run with `npx tsx`), a `dm`/MCP call or a screenshot, and record the command and its output in the evidence. Keep the scripts so the reviewer can rerun them; the testing tail turns them into tests and deletes them. Check in reusable fixture data where a criterion names fixtures. Build or launch the app (`npm run build`, `npm run dev`) only when a criterion needs the built CLI/MCP server or a real-app screenshot. Never run the full suite, coverage, whole-tree lint or Fireguard: report them `skipped` with "left to the testing tail". Use existing shared command and portable-state conventions; no direct .darkmechanicus record editing. Keep implementation inside this ticket's scope; coordinate shared interface files with the orchestrator. New module names may follow the repository convention.

Give the owner one place to see a folder's measured performance, reached from the sidebar.

**Link.** `src/renderer/src/sidebar/SidebarFooter.tsx` renders the MCP line (plug icon, `MCP`, session text) and then the export/Flush line. Add a new `footer-line` directly below the MCP line and above the export line: a link-styled button labelled `Metrics` with a new `chart` icon added to `ICON_PATHS` in `src/renderer/src/components/Icon.tsx`. Show it only when `folderReady`; set `aria-current="page"` while the dashboard is open; keep it keyboard-focusable. Pass `metricsOpen` and `onOpenMetrics` from `ShellFooter` in `src/renderer/src/App.tsx`, and include the `metrics` view in its `folderReady` test so the link and Flush stay visible while the dashboard is open.

**Navigation.** Add `{ kind: 'metrics'; folder }` to `MainView` in `src/renderer/src/app/chooseView.ts` and a folder-scoped metrics pane to `Selection` in `src/renderer/src/app/selection.ts`, following the `agentPane` pattern, so `isSelection`/`resolveSelection` persist and validate it. Add the action in `src/renderer/src/app/shellActions.ts`. `chooseView` shows the dashboard only for an available, initialized folder (the unavailable and onboarding views still win). Add an explicit `case 'metrics'` to `MainPane` in `App.tsx` (its `default` falls through to the folder pane, so a missing case still compiles). Selecting an epic, chat, agent or another folder leaves the dashboard.

**Drill-down.** `src/renderer/src/app/landing.ts` only lands on a ticket's Activity tab or a chat thread. Extend it with Scorecard-tab landings for a ticket and for an epic (the tabs from DM-180 and DM-181), handed over like the existing ticket landing.

**Dashboard.** New `src/renderer/src/metrics/MetricsDashboard.tsx` reads `getMetricsSummary` through `window.dm` (DM-265) with the `useResource` pattern and the shell refresh tick. It shows:
- a header with the policy version and data freshness/cutoff;
- summary tiles: grade-status distribution, total tokens with coverage, elapsed vs active vs waiting time, summed effort, corrective share;
- a per-epic table (grade with status, coverage, tokens, active and wall time) whose rows open that epic's Scorecard tab (DM-181);
- the sprint trend, with incomparable entries labelled;
- top gaps linking to the ticket Scorecard tab (DM-180).

Missing values read `unavailable`, never 0. An empty folder explains how measurements arrive (connect an agent over MCP). An error offers Retry. Reuse existing card, table and theme tokens in `styles.css`; add no charting dependency.

